# Consulted learnings — <project name>

> The *consume* side of the cross-project learning loop — produced via `prompts/consult.md` at project start (and refreshed when the work turns to a new stack, surface, or phase). It is the **read-in from the cold tier**: the learning pool is the cross-project analog of the store, and this driver — like every fresh context — is born without history. These are the few prior lessons whose tags matched this project, surfaced where the driver and its workers will look.
>
> **This is context, not a frozen deliverable.** It is not an audit and produces no work artifact. Nothing here is binding — it *informs*; `DECISIONS.md` still governs. A learning that shapes a decision is cited in that decision's rationale. Refresh this file freely as the work moves.

**Pool consulted:** <which pool — configured `LEARNINGS.md` paths / sibling-repo glob / user-level pool / enterprise index>
**Filter tags:** <this project's tags — stack · domain · phase — used to filter the pool's indexes>

> **If the pool was empty or nothing matched, say so plainly here and stop** — an empty pool is a valid, auditable result, never a silent skip. (e.g. "No pool configured yet — nothing consulted." / "Pool scanned; no index lines intersected the filter tags.")

